# nums-model: the second generation of NUMS.Go (the http/ module) as read and run on 2026-11-24. Sources are under 2.5.

n: 3.2
name: nums-model
kind: hub
is: NUMS.Go's http/ module at 9e6bbb4 (2023-04-05) parses Go with tree-sitter and relabels each syntax node from a 237-label tree rooted at Blueprint, Recipe and Cell, through one YAML table per language. It analyses code and executes none. Every id it allots is a counter or a position, and label ids change between runs. Nothing compiles as committed; in a patched copy 23 of 29 tests pass. A newer declaration/use model is mid-refactor and panics at HEAD. Only Go is mapped; five other grammars reach an auto-label worksheet.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

n: 3.2.1
name: model
kind: hub
is: The http/ module is an analysis program with two models in one package: a working one (Node_t, IdScope_t, global caches) and a newer interface model that crosses three roots with role bits, makes a package a blueprint plus a recipe and every expression a use of a built-in recipe, has 73 stub methods, copies generics shallowly and regressed at HEAD.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

n: 3.2.1.1
name: analysis-not-execution
kind: observation
is: NUMS.Go's http/ module (Go module <prefix>/http) parses Go source with tree-sitter and re-describes each syntax node in a vocabulary rooted at Blueprint (types), Recipe (behaviour) and Cell (storage). http/model holds no interpreter and no code emitter: the module analyses code and does not execute, emit or translate any.
status: observed
