name: name-is-identity
kind: finding
is: In the http/ generation of NUMS.Go a label's name is its identity and its number is a handle valid inside one process: an id written to the language JSON cache or served at /api/label/:id means something else in the next process. That is the reverse of a numeric space with names attached as a replaceable lens.
