n: 3.2.2.5
name: identifier-scope-record
kind: observation
is: IdScope_t is one record for an identifier and the scope it opens: ID, Name, Parent, Children by name, Properties (named pointers into the syntax tree), Position, Kind, Labels and four lists Calling, Reads, Writes, Uses of IdUse_t {ID, LoopLevel, Node}. ID is len(IdScopes)+1. Lookup searches the scope's children, then walks Parent upward.
