n: 3.2.3
name: lens
kind: hub
is: The neutral vocabulary is a YAML tree of 237 labels with inherited score, level, colour and operator templates. Go.yaml maps tree-sitter symbols to label sets many-to-many and carries naming, scoping, matching and looping rules over a small selector language. Labelling ends in pruning by context, so one symbol gets different labels by position.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

n: 3.2.3.1
name: label-tree
kind: observation
is: http/config/labels.yaml is 298 lines and defines 237 labels under 11 top-level entries, among them IdentifierKind, Recipe, Blueprint and Cell. Score, level, colour and attribute are inherited downward. The tree names constructs Go lacks (Ternary, While, Try/Catch/Throw, Malloc/Free, This/Super); only Go is mapped onto it.
status: observed
src: 2.5.16#1-298 2.5.5#104-159 2.5.29#104
