at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

n: 3.2.3.2
name: op-templates
kind: observation
is: A label in labels.yaml may carry _Op, a surface template with numbered holes, such as '{0} + {1}' and 'for {0}; {1}; {2} {3}'. The engine interprets it only as an arity that tells apart operators sharing one grammar symbol, and passes the string unchanged into label results and AsYaml; there is one template per label, not one per language.
status: observed
src: 2.5.16#79-207 2.5.5#569-587 2.5.6#1151-1168 2.5.2#287 2.5.2#300 2.5.19#229-234 2.5.5#74-76
limit: The unchanged string is the Op field of a label result (model.go:287 and :300), returned by GET_Labels (api.go:229-234), and the _Op key written by AsYaml (label.go:74-76). All 81 _Op lines of labels.yaml hold {0}, so a template that is present has an arity of at least one.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

n: 3.2.3.3
name: language-file
kind: observation
is: http/config/Go.yaml (282 lines) is the only language file. Its Labels section maps 112 labels to lists of grammar symbol names, many-to-many: '*' stands under five labels, among them Multiply and Pointer. Its 19 naming rules give Name, Names or NoName, Kind, Scope, Properties and Match over selectors such as $Named[i], $Field[name] and $Parent.
status: observed
