n: 3.2.4.4
name: queries-and-scores
kind: observation
is: api.go registers 14 JSON routes; /api/nodes builds a filter from 18 query parameters and returns only a histogram. A filter requires all requested labels; a result names the fields wanted plus a filter and field list for children. Symbol score is always 1, so its sum is the node count; a node's label score is the mean of its positive label scores.
status: observed
src: 2.5.19#358-389 2.5.19#194-222 2.5.30#152-246 2.5.6#1235-1320 2.5.6#244-259 2.5.2#755 2.5.29#52-59
limit: The server was not started. HotScore is a placeholder; formula scores and a query expression language are planned in the design note and absent in code; recipe write sets come out empty and HasExtern false. Node_t.MaxLabelLevel and MinLabelLevel both return 0 (query.go:152-153), so a MaxLabelLevel of 0 or more never rejects a node and a MinLabelLevel of 1 or more rejects every node (query.go:229-232).
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/nums-model

